# Values are plain: no quotes, no inline comments (scripts/lib/entry.sh reads them literally).
#
# Self-hosted install: `cp .env.example .env && docker compose up -d` in infra/compose. Compose
# reads this file for its settings; no service gets it as an env file (init-secrets mounts it
# only to read the CHELABASE_SEED_* lines). Every setting has a default in docker-compose.yml, so
# the copy runs as it is on one machine, at http://studio.chelabase.localhost:8000. Keep .env
# chmod 600 once it holds a seed or an SMTP setting. Do not commit it.
#
# Workbench: `just workbench up` renders each stack's `.chelabase/stacks/<slug>/env/stack.env`
# from this file plus the per-stack values (hosts and ports, service names, paths, images), and
# the stack's apps read that file and the stack's `zitadel/demo.env`. Only the settings below
# that aren't commented out reach it; edit this file to change a workbench default.

# --- The public entry (host settings) ---
# Everything a browser or client reaches goes through the gateway, by host name. Rules (checked
# at startup): each host is different; a port matches only that port, and never the scheme's
# default (80/443); the issuer is derived from the auth host and the scheme, so don't set
# CHELABASE_ZITADEL_ISSUER. Hosts are lowercase.
# http or https (blank or unset = https in the services; the compose default is http): the
# scheme of every public URL and X-Forwarded-Proto. Session cookies are Secure exactly when it is
# https (in every mode; CHELABASE_AUTH_SECURE_COOKIES overrides). Platform mode requires https.
# TLS ends in front of the gateway (docs: self-hosting/hosts).
CHELABASE_PUBLIC_SCHEME=http
# Studio web app. Same registrable domain as the API (SameSite=Strict cookies), not a public suffix
CHELABASE_STUDIO_HOST=studio.chelabase.localhost:8000
# Management API, data API and app-user sign-in. Same registrable domain as Studio
CHELABASE_API_HOST=api.chelabase.localhost:8000
# Zitadel, on its own host (its issuer and redirects are root paths); the issuer comes from it
CHELABASE_AUTH_HOST=auth.chelabase.localhost:8000
# Optional (blank = unset): the docs site, the landing page and Mailpit (workbench only)
CHELABASE_DOCS_HOST=docs.chelabase.localhost:8000
CHELABASE_LANDING_HOST=landing.chelabase.localhost:8000
CHELABASE_MAIL_HOST=mail.chelabase.localhost:8000
# Where a gateway run on the host listens (a list; *.localhost resolves to ::1 on some machines).
# The compose gateway listens on CHELABASE_PUBLIC_PORT inside its container instead.
CHELABASE_GATEWAY_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8000,[::1]:8000

# --- Self-hosted install: what Compose can't derive from the hosts ---
# Compose can't split a host into its name and port, so set these to match the three hosts
# whenever you change them (init-secrets checks they match and names the line to fix):
# the names without the port, the public port (the hosts' port, else 80 for http / 443 for
# https), true for https, and Zitadel's TLS mode (disabled for http, external for https).
# CHELABASE_STUDIO_HOST_NAME=studio.chelabase.localhost
# CHELABASE_API_HOST_NAME=api.chelabase.localhost
# CHELABASE_AUTH_HOST_NAME=auth.chelabase.localhost
# CHELABASE_PUBLIC_PORT=8000
# CHELABASE_PUBLIC_SECURE=false
# CHELABASE_ZITADEL_TLS_MODE=disabled
# Where the host publishes the gateway: the address (0.0.0.0 for every interface, e.g. behind
# your own TLS proxy on another machine) and the port (default: CHELABASE_PUBLIC_PORT).
# CHELABASE_HTTP_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# CHELABASE_HTTP_PORT=8000
# Reverse proxies in front of the gateway whose X-Forwarded-For (or Forwarded) it believes:
# comma-separated CIDRs or addresses, as the gateway sees the proxy (blank: none; the client is
# the TCP peer). See the hosts page, "Behind a reverse proxy". A proxy on this machine that
# connects to the published port is seen at the Docker network's gateway address: the "Gateway"
# that `docker network inspect <project>_default` prints (the project is this directory's name,
# `compose`, unless you set another). List that one address, not a range.
# CHELABASE_GATEWAY_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.18.0.1
# The release images: registry prefix and tag. Each image is pinned by digest in the compose
# file; setting either variable replaces that pin (a tag without a digest is not verified).
# CHELABASE_IMAGE_REPO=ghcr.io/chelabase
# CHELABASE_IMAGE_TAG=
# The pinned images (written by scripts/pin-images.sh, checked by scripts/tests/compose-image-pins.sh):
# BEGIN image pins
# ghcr.io/chelabase/gateway:7c0297be4237@sha256:fa8aedef85fc50182ac6045a068693fedcf649b85a4318b91cd95e7ad9cd5a4d
# ghcr.io/chelabase/orchestrator:7c0297be4237@sha256:dadacedd0253ce5b234a4c44b86830d22b8c42e9855cd68e9787643b9c56b1eb
# ghcr.io/chelabase/worker:7c0297be4237@sha256:26f7d7d2fa8439e01638651f0168a5b28591e1803f046419416d4466e5c67cc4
# ghcr.io/chelabase/rest:7c0297be4237@sha256:f351986cc25124b2077a8a617e69f85d9ac106eca05005b450b0de909a90f945
# ghcr.io/chelabase/auth:7c0297be4237@sha256:e2b7a2285689c065f53a9f40ff1b6b966f65da1a5f2cebe0af89908b505ce6aa
# ghcr.io/chelabase/realtime:7c0297be4237@sha256:c913c2ba7d310c44a296cb257b895ff43990d58175b97f371c8526d8fd293ff5
# ghcr.io/chelabase/init:7c0297be4237@sha256:a893bd91643abac68df58c4cefda463d4c67024a2e4301b1e7044f8b13cf2c18
# ghcr.io/chelabase/studio:7c0297be4237@sha256:3ea1424c0cbac44ef2ca3cfbc63c27164bf27c535df08cf8312ebc52cbd95fff
# END image pins
# The control network the orchestrator and realtime reach computes on, and their static
# addresses in it (change it when it overlaps a network of the host; computes use the upper /23).
# CHELABASE_CONTROL_SUBNET=10.214.0.0/22
# CHELABASE_CONTROL_COMPUTE_RANGE=10.214.2.0/23
# CHELABASE_ORCHESTRATOR_CONTROL_IP=10.214.0.10
# CHELABASE_REALTIME_CONTROL_IP=10.214.0.12
# Where clients connect to databases: the proxy, at <endpoint>.CHELABASE_PROXY_DOMAIN on
# CHELABASE_PROXY_PORT (Postgres) and CHELABASE_PROXY_HTTP_PORT (SQL over HTTP), published on
# CHELABASE_PROXY_ADDR. Connection details in Studio and the API name the same host and port.
# The proxy routes a connection by that host name (TLS SNI), so every <endpoint>.<domain> must
# reach this machine: the default localtest.me resolves to 127.0.0.1 everywhere, for local use;
# on a server, set a domain whose wildcard record points at it (*.db.example.com) and
# CHELABASE_PROXY_ADDR=0.0.0.0. The certificate (*.<domain>) is issued by the install's own CA;
# clients verify with it: `docker compose cp proxy:/tls/ca.crt proxy-ca.crt`. 5432 is the
# Postgres default; change it when the host runs its own Postgres.
# CHELABASE_PROXY_DOMAIN=localtest.me
# CHELABASE_PROXY_ADDR=127.0.0.1
# CHELABASE_PROXY_PORT=5432
# CHELABASE_PROXY_HTTP_PORT=4444
# The worker and the orchestrator join the Docker socket's group (read from the socket at
# start), so no Docker gid is configured.

# --- Self-hosted install: SMTP (optional) ---
# Zitadel's emails (invites, password resets). Unset: no SMTP. The password is read from a file
# on the host (never put it here): CHELABASE_SMTP_PASSWORD_PATH, mounted into the bootstrap only.
# The bootstrap reads it as uid 10001 (groups 10001 and 70), so the file must be owned by uid
# 10001 at mode 0600 (`sudo chown 10001 <file> && sudo chmod 600 <file>`), or 0640 with one of
# those groups; a looser file, or one it can't read, fails init-bootstrap naming the file.
# A changed setting or password is applied by the next `docker compose up`.
# CHELABASE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# CHELABASE_SMTP_PORT=587
# CHELABASE_SMTP_FROM=chelabase@example.com
# CHELABASE_SMTP_USER=chelabase
# CHELABASE_SMTP_PASSWORD_PATH=/etc/chelabase/smtp.password

# --- Self-hosted install: chosen secret values (optional) ---
# Chosen secret values (optional). chelabase-init writes each one as its secret file on the
# FIRST run only, instead of generating it; they never enter any container's environment.
# Once a file exists, a different value here makes init fail (rotation: chelabase/chelabase#6).
# Values: printable ASCII, no spaces, quotes, backslash, backtick or $; up to 1024 characters;
# passwords and tokens at least 16; the masterkey exactly 32. Keep this file chmod 600.
# Each seed sets the secret of the same name, except two: CHELABASE_SEED_APP_AUTH_TOKEN is
# CHELABASE_APP_AUTH_INTERNAL_TOKEN, CHELABASE_SEED_APP_SESSIONS_TOKEN is
# CHELABASE_APP_SESSIONS_INTERNAL_TOKEN.
# CHELABASE_SEED_METADATA_DB_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_ZITADEL_DB_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_ZITADEL_DB_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_STORCON_DB_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_S3_ACCESS_KEY=
# CHELABASE_SEED_S3_SECRET_KEY=
# CHELABASE_SEED_ZITADEL_MASTERKEY=
# CHELABASE_SEED_NATS_ORCHESTRATOR_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_NATS_WORKER_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_NATS_REALTIME_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_NATS_RUNNER_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_VALKEY_PROXY_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_VALKEY_CONTROL_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_VALKEY_REALTIME_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_VALKEY_RUNNER_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_VALKEY_HEALTH_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_REALTIME_PG_PASSWORD=
# CHELABASE_SEED_REALTIME_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
# CHELABASE_SEED_REST_INTERNAL_TOKEN=
# CHELABASE_SEED_DATA_KEYS_TOKEN=
# CHELABASE_SEED_APP_AUTH_TOKEN=
# CHELABASE_SEED_APP_SESSIONS_TOKEN=
# CHELABASE_SEED_PROXY_API_TOKEN=
# CHELABASE_SEED_STORCON_HOOK_TOKEN=

# --- Mode ---
# self-hosted: what runs today. platform: the hosted cloud (not built yet). Services refuse to
# start on any other value. A self-hosted install always runs self-hosted (docker-compose.yml
# sets it; this line doesn't reach it): only the workbench reads this line.
CHELABASE_MODE=self-hosted
# Email verification of Studio sign-ups (when a tenant switches open sign-up on) and of app users'
# sign-up follows the mode: off in self-hosted (accounts are created verified), required in platform. Set true/false to override; codes land in Mailpit locally.
# CHELABASE_REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION=

# --- Zitadel (workbench) ---
# The token audiences: a workbench stack's demo.env sets them (the project id and the API app's
# client id). Otherwise each service reads CHELABASE_ZITADEL_PROJECT_ID(_FILE) and
# CHELABASE_ZITADEL_API_CLIENT_ID(_FILE), the bootstrap's output files in a self-hosted install.
# An empty list accepts no token (every Zitadel bearer is refused); it never means "any".
CHELABASE_ZITADEL_AUDIENCES=
# CHELABASE_ZITADEL_INTERNAL_URL is not read from this file: docker-compose.yml sets it to
# http://zitadel:8080 for every app (their calls to Zitadel stay inside the network, with the
# auth host as Host; a token's iss is still the public issuer). A service run on the host on its
# own reads it from its environment: an http(s)://host[:port] origin, unset = the issuer.
# CHELABASE_DEMO_TOKEN is not stored — mint with: cargo run -q -p chelabase -- dev token
# Machine key: demo-sa.json in the stack's zitadel state directory (from chelabase dev bootstrap)

# --- Settings of a service run on its own (the defaults; Compose sets service-name ones) ---
# CHELABASE_METADATA_DATABASE_URL=postgres://chelabase@127.0.0.1:5433/chelabase_metadata
#   (its password from CHELABASE_METADATA_DATABASE_PASSWORD_FILE)
# CHELABASE_NATS_URL=nats://127.0.0.1:4222
# CHELABASE_ORCHESTRATOR_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8081
# CHELABASE_WORKER_HEALTH_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8082
# CHELABASE_INTERNAL_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8083
# CHELABASE_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8083
# CHELABASE_AUTH_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8084
# CHELABASE_REST_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8085
# CHELABASE_REST_INTERNAL_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8086
# Realtime: its public listener (behind the gateway) and its internal one (/health only).
# CHELABASE_REALTIME_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8087
# CHELABASE_REALTIME_INTERNAL_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8088
# CHELABASE_VALKEY_URL=redis://127.0.0.1:6379
# Valkey over TLS (rediss://): off in a stack, on in platform mode.
# CHELABASE_VALKEY_TLS=off
# CHELABASE_CONTROL_PLANE_URI=http://host.docker.internal:8083
# The gateway's upstreams.
# CHELABASE_ORCHESTRATOR_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081
# CHELABASE_REALTIME_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8087
# CHELABASE_GATEWAY_UPSTREAM_TIMEOUT_SECS=60

# --- Proxy CA file ---
# Only the file name reported as `ca_file` in the connection details (sslrootcert=<it>); it
# doesn't change which CA the proxy uses. A self-hosted install's default is proxy-ca.crt, the
# file `docker compose cp proxy:/tls/ca.crt proxy-ca.crt` writes; a workbench stack sets
# <stack dir>/neon/proxy-ca.crt; a service run on its own defaults to .chelabase/neon/proxy-ca.crt.
# CHELABASE_PROXY_CA_FILE=proxy-ca.crt

# --- Database credentials ---
# CHELABASE_SECRETS_KEY is the path to the key that encrypts database passwords at rest
# (secrets/secrets.key in the secrets volume; a workbench's keys dir). Never rotate or delete
# it: stored passwords can't be decrypted without it.
# Self-hosted only (ignored in platform mode): true → new databases' `postgres` owner role
# is a real SUPERUSER. Users can then alter `cloud_admin` or `neon_superuser` and break the
# compute's reconfigure (compute_ctl) and the worker's admin SQL for that database.
# CHELABASE_DB_OWNER_SUPERUSER=false
# Read by the orchestrator and the worker.
# Most login roles per branch, the owner not counted (default 50, allowed 0..=500).
# CHELABASE_BRANCH_ROLE_CAP=50
# Most databases per branch, the system `postgres` database not counted (default 20,
# allowed 1..=1000).
# CHELABASE_BRANCH_DATABASE_CAP=20
# Most databases a branch serves through the data API, the main database included (orchestrator
# only; default 10, allowed 1..=100). Over it, enabling a database answers 409.
# CHELABASE_BRANCH_DATA_API_DATABASE_CAP=10
# Password strength for passwords set in SQL: "on" or "off" (default "off" in self-hosted
# mode; platform mode always checks).
# CHELABASE_PASSWORD_STRENGTH=off

# --- Service credentials (generated; never in this file or stack.env) ---
# chelabase-init (init-secrets; `just workbench up` in a workbench) creates each one once
# (never overwritten, 0600 or 0640 with its reader's group) and only the services that read it
# mount it, getting its path as <NAME>_FILE:
#   nats/<user>.password      NATS users orchestrator, worker, realtime, runner (no anonymous access)
#   valkey/<user>.password    Valkey ACL users proxy, control, realtime, runner, health
#   tokens/*.token            the internal bearers: CHELABASE_REST_INTERNAL_TOKEN,
#                             CHELABASE_DATA_KEYS_TOKEN, CHELABASE_APP_AUTH_INTERNAL_TOKEN,
#                             CHELABASE_APP_SESSIONS_INTERNAL_TOKEN, CHELABASE_PROXY_API_TOKEN,
#                             CHELABASE_STORCON_HOOK_TOKEN
#   realtime/*                realtime's Postgres password, ticket key and internal bearer
#   neon/storage-tokens/*.jwt the storage services' NeonJWTs, signed with the compute-JWT key pair
#   db/*, s3/*, zitadel/*     the databases' passwords, the object store's keys, Zitadel's
#                             masterkey and steps file (a workbench keeps its fixed dev values)
# A service run apart from a stack reads <NAME> or <NAME>_FILE; unset, a bearer falls back to
# a public development value, which every service refuses unless CHELABASE_DEV_DEFAULTS=1.

# --- Neon storage and proxy ---
# The pageserver, the three safekeepers and the storage controller require NeonJWT (no --dev).
# STORCON_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1234
# CHELABASE_STORCON_URL=http://127.0.0.1:1234
# Safekeeper HTTP API by storage-controller id (`id=url`, comma separated); the worker reads
# each timeline's commit LSN from here. Default: one safekeeper on 127.0.0.1:7676.
# CHELABASE_SAFEKEEPER_HTTP=1=http://127.0.0.1:7676

# --- App users (docs site, /docs/using/app-users) ---
# Access token lifetime, seconds (auth; 60..=86400)
# CHELABASE_APP_ACCESS_TTL_SECS=900
# Refresh token sliding lifetime, seconds (orchestrator; at most 90 days)
# CHELABASE_APP_REFRESH_TTL_SECS=2592000
# How often the worker reconciles each enabled project's users, seconds (30..=86400)
# CHELABASE_APP_USERS_RECONCILE_SECS=300
# How often the worker reconciles every branch's member roles, seconds (30..=86400): the
# backstop for reconcile requests lost on NATS or whose retries all failed
# CHELABASE_MEMBER_ROLES_SWEEP_SECS=300
# How often the worker checks in Zitadel that each member with a live personal login is still
# active, seconds (1..=86400)
# CHELABASE_IDENTITY_SWEEP_SECS=600
# Platform mode only (a self-hosted install doesn't pass it): the Zitadel organization whose
# members administer the instance (/v1/instance/settings); nobody passes while it is unset.
# CHELABASE_OPERATOR_ORG_ID=
# Worker reconcile removes compute containers with no endpoint row; false logs and keeps them.
# The worker only lists computes labelled with its own stack (CHELABASE_STACK: the Compose
# project in a self-hosted install), so this switch is not what keeps stacks apart.
# CHELABASE_WORKER_REMOVE_ORPHANS=true
